THOUGHT: I need to make getEntities(RenderType) null-safe by handling the case where miscEntities.get(renderType) returns null, ideally mirroring patterns elsewhere (e.g., returning an empty collection). I’ll implement that change with sed, then run the Gradle compile to ensure the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '1138,1140c\  public Collection<IEntity> getEntities(final RenderType renderType) {
    Map<Integer, IEntity> entitiesByRenderType = this.miscEntities.get(renderType);
    if (entitiesByRenderType == null) {
      return Collections.emptySet();
    }

    return Collections.unmodifiableCollection(entitiesByRenderType.values());
  }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/environment/Environment.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|error[s]?$" new_build_output.log | tail -n 20
